52	    5. runs `bash <shared run directory>/harness/fetch_private.sh` as `cmp-eval` (as a part runs, below) with working directory `cmp-private` and `HOME` and `TMPDIR` set to `cmp-private/.home` (created empty, removed afterwards), then cleans up after `cmp-eval` (below); a nonzero exit fails;
53	    6. fails when `cmp-private` holds anything other than regular files and directories, and otherwise makes it and everything under it owned by `root` with group `cmp-eval`, with directories at mode `750` and files at mode `640`, so the evaluator can read and never change it;
54	    7. fails when any regular file in the shared run directory outside `cmp-private`, or under the box user's home directory, has the size and SHA-256 of a regular file under `cmp-private`;
55	    8. checks that `sudo -n -u <user> nvidia-smi -L` prints, for each of the two users, the same number of GPU lines as for the box user, that `sudo -n -u cmp-arm test -r cmp-private` fails, and that the two rules of step 2 are present (`iptables -C`, `ip6tables -C`).
56	    Any failure fails evaluate with `error_class: infra` before any invocation. Cleanup after a part user is: kill every process of the user (`pkill -KILL -u <user>`) once per second until `pgrep -u <user>` finds none, for at most the time left in `budget_s`; delete every entry the user owns below each directory listed for it in `profiler/cmp_writable.json` (`find <dir> -mindepth 1 -user <user> -delete`); and remove every System V IPC object the user owns. The arm part therefore cannot read the evaluator's private data or anything the evaluator left behind, cannot reach the network, cannot write any file the evaluator or the wrapper runs, and cannot change modes that protect them, whatever its adapter or commands do.
57	  - Versions: one box command, operation `versions`, runs `bash harness/versions.sh` with stdout to `out/comparison/versions.json`, then the trusted `python3 profiler/cmp_system.py` (written inline by the pipeline) writes `out/comparison/system.json`, exactly `{cpu_model, cpu_logical, kernel, driver_version, cuda_version, gpus, executables}`: `lscpu` model name and logical CPU count; `uname -r`; the driver and CUDA versions that `nvidia-smi` reports; `gpus` one row per GPU, exactly `{index, name, uuid, memory_total}`, from `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,name,uuid,memory.total --format=csv,noheader`; and `executables` mapping each key of `versions.json` to exactly `{version, executable, sha256, libraries}`, with `sha256` the SHA-256 of the executable's resolved file and `libraries` one row per `ldd` line of the form `<name> => <absolute path> ...`, exactly `{name, path, sha256}` (the resolved file's SHA-256), or `[]` when `ldd` fails or reports a static executable. Any field that cannot be read is null.

